## Gaps

I did not find an independently retrievable public-domain or open-access **numeric downward-height-percentile-line trigger** for short-stature work-up that matched the way NICE gives a parent-centile-distance trigger; the open sources I found were either narrative or institutional rather than a single public guideline table. citeturn5search0turn20view0turn23view2

I did not find an official CDC or WHO **numeric BMI-percentile trajectory-crossing cut-off** analogous to the category thresholds above; the public guideline sources were strong on category boundaries and chart-selection thresholds, but not on a canonical percentile-crossing rule. citeturn21view1turn24view0

For **Nellhaus raw chart-table thresholds**, the original 1968 *Pediatrics* article is rights-restricted/paywalled, so I did not extract raw chart values from the original source. I used open secondary sources for older-child chart selection and one study-specific Nellhaus percentile criterion instead. citeturn7search2turn9search1turn9search0

I did not re-extract **INTERGROWTH-21st preterm corrected-age thresholds** because your prompt explicitly marked the preterm/VLBW corrected-age branch as already held and out of scope for re-derivation.